In accordance with the President’s decision, the hearing took place in public in the Human Rights Building, Strasbourg, on 2 February 1982. The Court had held a preparatory meeting beforehand. There appeared before the Court:

for the Government Mr J.L. Read, Assistant Under-Secretary for Legal Affairs, Ministry for Foreign Affairs, Agent, Mr H. Hudson, Under-Secretary, Ministry of Justice, Adviser;

for the Commission Mr K. Jones, Delegate;

for the applicant Mr T. Taylor, advokat, Counsel. The Court heard addresses by Mr Cox, Mr Cook and Mr Young, as well as replies to a question put by it.

